                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "what do you mean by terminal completion?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "Addressed in Patch Set 2. Clarified this as the final successful fetch completion path when nextRecordHandle == 0."
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we name this resetPDRProcessingState() to match the uppercase PDR everywhere?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "Addressed in Patch Set 2. Renamed to resetPDRProcessingState() for naming consistency with PDR usage in this file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 496,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this handles the case where we have stale entries? (I mean duplicate entries) In every fetch cycle?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 496,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, line 496 clears the buffered per-fetch state, but the motivation for this patch is to remove the function-static state entirely. The change makes that temporary state instance-scoped, with explicit reset points, so the behavior is easier to reason about and no longer depends on hidden static locals."
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 528,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "This only clears the state sensors and FRU record set PDRs; what happens to the entity association PDRs then?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 528,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for raising this. In this flow, Entity Association PDRs are processed differently from State Sensor/FRU PDRs: they are merged into the entity tree immediately when each Entity Association record is received, not buffered in per-fetch pending containers.\nThis patch only moves the previous function-static per-fetch state to instance scope (merge flag + pending State Sensor PDR list + pending FRU Record Set PDR list).\nSo, behavior for Entity Association merge is unchanged by this patch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 685,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is an extra variable needed here? Can't we use mergedHostPdrs directly in line 694?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "host-bmc/host_pdr_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 685,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Meghana Vangapandu",
                        "email": "meghanav@ami.com",
                        "username": "MeghanaVangapandu0"
                    },
                    "message": "We cannot use mergedHostPdrs directly there because it is cleared by resetPDRProcessingState(). The local variable preserves the current-cycle result so we can still decide whether to send the PDR repository changed event afterward."
                }
            ],
